 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Gating
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object: `{ metric_id: min_value }`.
+- Thresholds enable CI/CD gating: exit 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass, 2 for usage errors.
+- Metrics without scores (e.g., exact match without references) fail their threshold by design.
+- Report includes `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array of objects with metric, min, score, passed) for structured consumption.
+- Markdown reports display a "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status for each threshold.
+- Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`; no changes to metric signatures required.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
