 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
+### Evaluation with Thresholds (SDK)
+
+Use `Eval.generateReport` with the `thresholds` option to gate evaluations on metric scores:
+
+```js
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({
+  outputs: modelOutputs,
+  references: goldStandard
+});
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: 'outputs.json',
+  referencesPath: 'references.json',
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+// report.passed is true if all thresholds pass
+// report.thresholds is an array of { metric, min, score, passed }
+console.log(`Evaluation ${report.passed ? 'passed' : 'failed'}`);
+
+await Eval.writeReport({
+  report,
+  format: 'json',
+  reportPath: 'eval-report.json'
+});
+```
+
+Thresholds work with custom metrics too. If a metric has no score (e.g., `exact_match` without references), it fails its threshold.
+
